   "id": "D-019-R007",
   "text": "The independent reviewer must begin from the directive and actual code (not the producer's conclusions), use a fresh clean worktree pinned to the submitted SHA, create new adversarial probes not copied from producer tests, trace actual imports and calls for every claimed integration, execute all documented commands exactly, test clean/dirty/committed/uncommitted/missing/malformed/hostile states, attempt to exploit every observation (including defects labeled pre-existing or low probability), reject proxy proof (field presence, source/test counts) when semantic correctness is required, and mark FAIL if any literal directive guarantee is contradicted; a review observation affecting a required guarantee is blocking and cannot be downgraded because the code predates this task.",
